      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks like an error.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is double the usual maximum for immediate-release metformin, which is 2,550 mg/day (2,000 mg/day for extended-release). At that dose the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity goes up, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals**, which is 2,550 mg/day, the maximum.\n- **1000 mg PO twice daily with meals**, which is 2,000 mg/day.\n- **500 mg PO three times daily with meals**, which is 1,500 mg/day.\n- **1700 mg per day** in total, for example 850 mg twice daily.\n\nIf 1700 mg three times daily is what you want, tell me and I'll enter it with a note recording that you confirmed the dose. Otherwise, tell me the dose and frequency you want and I'll enter that."
      }
